       "text": "The AI lobby is not spending millions to sway politicians on the virtues of a foreign government that is, according to many observers, committing genocide. But it is fronting a movement that is no longer very popular. A recent Quinnipiac University poll found that only 35 percent of Americans are “very excited” or “somewhat excited” about artificial intelligence. A vast majority, 62 percent, are either “not so excited” (29 percent) or “not excited at all” (33 percent) about AI. When asked about how concerned they are, respondents are unequivocal: 80 percent are either “very concerned” (38 percent) or “somewhat concerned” (42 percent) about AI. Concern, as measured by Quinnipiac, cuts across age groups. Gen Z’s “very concerned” (35 percent) hardly differs from the baby-boomers’ 39 percent.",
