       "tag": "p",
       "text": "Had the weather been merely seasonal after the snow fell, Mamdani would have received his kudos and skipped along to February. Instead, New York and much of the Northeast endured the most brutal cold in decades. For nine consecutive days , the temperature didn’t climb above freezing. Though this did not technically break a record — in 2018, New York temperatures remained at or below freezing for 14 consecutive days — the lows were in the single digits with horrifying windchill. Large portions of the city waterways iced over completely.",
