       "inline": "For them, Mamdani’s original sin was his appointment of Jessica Tisch as police commissioner. Tisch is, unlike Mamdani, both a political moderate and a proud Zionist. The Tisch-Mamdani alliance appears firm enough, even if small fissures are beginning to emerge. Police complaints about Mamdani’s more [-deliberated-]{+deliberate+} response to a recent pair of NYPD-involved shootings sounded suspiciously like leaks that could have come from Tisch’s office. But [-Mamdani-]{+the mayor+}, for now, has her back, and most of his base has remained accepting of this reality. Given that Mamdani has promised to govern as a democratic socialist and has stood by the leftists in his government, including the embattled Cea Weaver , there is plenty {+of +}reason to believe he’s earnest and not tacking to the center in [-the-]{+a+} way that would[- fully-] alienate his most fervent backers."
