       "text": "It is overly simplistic to fully blame Buttigieg for a disaster that was, first and foremost, a catastrophic failure for Norfolk Southern, the rail company. Buttigieg this week announced a package of reforms that would, if implemented, bolster rail safety. But far too much of the response — from communication to cleanup — has been outsourced to a private company that has unnerved locals. The company’s decision to undertake a “controlled burning” to release the hazardous chemicals into the air has led to fears that it could harm residents’ health both in the near and long term. The EPA maintains that air and water tests show no hazard to residents, but government officials can get things wrong and they can lie. They maintained the water was safe to drink in Flint until it was not, and that there was no risk from the debris right after 9/11 before thousands came down with cancer. The residents of East Palestine are entitled to their paranoia.",
