       "text": "The downfall of Roe v. Wade in June offered Democrats a singular opportunity to argue for why electing them actually matters, yet there are also numerous factors working against them that Cortez Masto, who is very much reflective of the median center-left Democrat in Washington, must overcome. The president’s party almost always loses seats in a midterm year. Worries over persistently high inflation remain. Wages in Nevada have not kept up with surging home prices. Though Las Vegas has rebounded from the depths of the pandemic, the tourism-based economy has struggled to bounce back. Biden, despite a recent bump in his approval ratings , is still not very popular.",
